    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "DNG Ivan Connaughton are delighted to present this impressive five-bedroom detached residence, extending to approximately 2,823 sq. ft. and standing on a beautifully maintained site of c. 0.70 acres at Gorteen, Mountbellew, Co. Galway, H53 KH21.\nOffering exceptionally spacious and versatile accommodation, this superb family home is presented in excellent condition throughout. The residence combines spacious and well-appointed living areas with five bedrooms, three en-suite facilities and a converted attic, making it ideally suited to a growing family or those working from home.\nThe property is approached via a tarmac driveway which extends to a detached garage of approximately 340 sq. ft. A distinctive stone façade, landscaped lawns and neatly maintained boundaries create an attractive first impression. To the rear, a large paved patio area provides an ideal setting for outdoor dining and entertaining, while the grounds enjoy pleasant views across the surrounding countryside.\nInternally, a bright and welcoming entrance hallway leads to a spacious living room featuring timber flooring and an attractive fireplace. The heart of the home is the impressive kitchen/dining room, fitted with an extensive range of units, ample worktop space and a central island. Double doors open into a light-filled sunroom overlooking the gardens, creating an inviting space in which to relax and enjoy the countryside views. The ground-floor accommodation also includes a large double bedroom and an adjoining shower room, which is also accessible from the large utility room.\nAt first-floor level, a spacious landing provides access to four large bedrooms and the family bathroom. Two of the bedrooms benefit from en-suite shower rooms, with the principal bedroom also featuring a walk-in wardrobe. The remaining bedrooms are bright and spacious, providing excellent accommodation for family members or guests. A further staircase leads to the converted attic level, comprising two versatile rooms suitable for additional storage.\nSituated in the peaceful countryside of Gorteen, the property enjoys a private rural setting just a short drive from Mountbellew. The town offers an excellent range of local amenities, including primary and secondary schools, shops, cafés, sporting facilities and the renowned Mountbellew Agricultural College. Galway City is approximately 45 minutes away, making the property a practical option for those commuting to the city while seeking the space and tranquillity of countryside living. Roscommon Town, Tuam and Ballinasloe are also within convenient driving distance.\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire an exceptionally spacious and well-appointed family residence occupying a substantial site in an attractive East Galway location.\nViewing is highly recommended.\nFor further details or to arrange a viewing, contact DNG Ivan Connaughton on 090-6663700."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Notice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> 7,000 litre underground rainwater harvesting system with a three filter and UV treatment system </li><li> Large Array of Thermal Solar on a south facing roof providing year round hot water </li><li> B rated - which will increase to A rated with the installation of a standard PV array on the roof </li><li> High efficiency indoor kerosene fired boiler </li><li> Integrated BEAM central vacuum system </li><li> 1GB Fibre broadband connection - CAT6 network cabling throughout all levels of the residence </li><li> High standard of attic insulation - over 12 inches of insulation to the eaves </li><li> Alarm system fitted with a GSM dialler </li><li> Powerful 250-watt LED exterior lighting, providing a versatile outdoor area during darker evenings </li><li> Directly adjacent to Carrownagappul Bog offering an attractive setting for walking</li></ul>"
      },
